{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008825-question-about-dreamspeaker-excerpt","id":1008825,"title":"Question about Dreamspeaker excerpt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T22:44:02-08:00","id":1008825,"title":"Question about Dreamspeaker excerpt","content":"The dreamspeaker tradition book has the following excerpt:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/xfBzNwF.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/xfBzNwF.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/xfBzNwF.png\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i.imgur.com/xfBzNwF.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm curious - the same tradition book says that you can have spirit allies and a spirit totem. So my question is, would you still have to use the spirit command on your spirit allies/your totems, or would they automatically do what you do in exchange for something?<br /> <br /> I don't understand. Here is a link so you could better help me understand this <span style=\"color:red\">please don't post links to entire books of Onyx Path material.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-27-2016, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T02:53:40-08:00","id":1008865,"title":"","content":"If you have to control or command a spirit, chances are you're not on good terms.<br /> <br /> If, however, they are your friends, then it's pretty much like getting any other NPC to do things for you. If it's achieving a common goal then they'll probably do it because it's mutually beneficial. If it's only going to help you though, they'll probably want something in return. Either that or they are repaying you for something you've already done to them.<br /> <br /> Point is, they aren't your allies if you have to command them. Or at least they may not be for long.<br /> <br /> For totems, as long as you abide by their bans and not do anything that would piss them off, you shouldn't have to control them in order to get their aid. Just roll Totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-27-2016, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T11:51:17-08:00","id":1008989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008825-question-about-dreamspeaker-excerpt?p=1008865#post1008865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have to control or command a spirit, chances are you're not on good terms.<br /> <br /> If, however, they are your friends, then it's pretty much like getting any other NPC to do things for you. If it's achieving a common goal then they'll probably do it because it's mutually beneficial. If it's only going to help you though, they'll probably want something in return. Either that or they are repaying you for something you've already done to them.<br /> <br /> Point is, they aren't your allies if you have to command them. Or at least they may not be for long.<br /> <br /> For totems, as long as you abide by their bans and not do anything that would piss them off, you shouldn't have to control them in order to get their aid. Just roll Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would I need to roll to get the aid of my spirit allies, as opposed to my totems?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:04:33-08:00","id":1008992,"title":"","content":"If they already want to do what you want them to do, then probably just a Spirit 2 effect to send a message, call them to you, or speak their language.<br /> <br /> If they don't then you'd have to add to that a few charisma/manipulation and expression rolls, depending on what you'd ask of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 11-28-2016, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T13:34:38-08:00","id":1009033,"title":"","content":"If you're looking at Spirit Command, I'm going to assume you're playing a Linear Shaman rather than a full mage. As such, how you contact spirits and entreat them is going to be very variable based on your character's approach to such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T16:40:02-08:00","id":1009083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008825-question-about-dreamspeaker-excerpt?p=1009033#post1009033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking at Spirit Command, I'm going to assume you're playing a Linear Shaman rather than a full mage. As such, how you contact spirits and entreat them is going to be very variable based on your character's approach to such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now what if I'm a full mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T20:22:49-08:00","id":1009143,"title":"","content":"Then see the above about Spirit 2 being used to call and communicate with the spirits in question. At that point, negotiations begin. You gain Spirit Allies in much the same way you win mundane Allies. You make friends (or in this case, a Pact), and agree to a mutually beneficial relationship. You do things for the spirit, and the spirit will do things for you. A fire spirit might agree to burn things when you ask them to (although a fire spirit would probably do that anyway), in return for you lighting one fire every day. A spirit of forgetfulness might mess with people's memory for you, if you agree to regularly take people's written or typed notes and destroy them (thereby eliminating the possibility for their owners to remember whatever they wrote down).<br /> <br /> A Totem's patronage is gained more or less the same way. It's just that the negotiations process is significantly more involved. Especially since the Totem will want any potential followers to manifest qualities in themselves that the resonate with that Totem. Coyote wants clever tricksters. Owl wants wisdom (even though real life owls are quite stupid). Spider might require patience. And that might mean going to great lengths to make those qualities part of the Mage's person. Spider, for instance, may not be willing to discuss the matter until the Mage has gone to its lair, sat on its web, and waited patiently without moving every day for a year.<br /> <br /> Oh right, I forgot to mention. Totems don't take the being called by upstart Mages. Spirits in general prefer not to have to go out of their way in this regard (&quot;Calling&quot; a spirit is literally what it sounds like; you call, and the spirit has to make the trip themselves). If you want a Totem to take you seriously, you have to use Spirit 3 and travel to them. Because they're kind of big deals in the spirit world. They have busy schedules, and things to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T08:39:01-08:00","id":1009344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008825-question-about-dreamspeaker-excerpt?p=1009143#post1009143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then see the above about Spirit 2 being used to call and communicate with the spirits in question. At that point, negotiations begin. You gain Spirit Allies in much the same way you win mundane Allies. You make friends (or in this case, a Pact), and agree to a mutually beneficial relationship. You do things for the spirit, and the spirit will do things for you. A fire spirit might agree to burn things when you ask them to (although a fire spirit would probably do that anyway), in return for you lighting one fire every day. A spirit of forgetfulness might mess with people's memory for you, if you agree to regularly take people's written or typed notes and destroy them (thereby eliminating the possibility for their owners to remember whatever they wrote down).<br /> <br /> A Totem's patronage is gained more or less the same way. It's just that the negotiations process is significantly more involved. Especially since the Totem will want any potential followers to manifest qualities in themselves that the resonate with that Totem. Coyote wants clever tricksters. Owl wants wisdom (even though real life owls are quite stupid). Spider might require patience. And that might mean going to great lengths to make those qualities part of the Mage's person. Spider, for instance, may not be willing to discuss the matter until the Mage has gone to its lair, sat on its web, and waited patiently without moving every day for a year.<br /> <br /> Oh right, I forgot to mention. Totems don't take the being called by upstart Mages. Spirits in general prefer not to have to go out of their way in this regard (&amp;quot;Calling&amp;quot; a spirit is literally what it sounds like; you call, and the spirit has to make the trip themselves). If you want a Totem to take you seriously, you have to use Spirit 3 and travel to them. Because they're kind of big deals in the spirit world. They have busy schedules, and things to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would I need forces to be able to call upon and utilize a fire spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T11:31:06-08:00","id":1009411,"title":"","content":"No, but it has many of the same drawbacks as paying an arsonist to start a fire for you. Most importantly that you do not have the control that using Forces and doing it yourself (even if in your Focus you're calling on the power of spirits to do things) would grant you.<br /> <br /> As well, one of the things that's supposed to balance actually calling on spirits to do things vs. invoking spirits are part of your Focus and using your Spheres is that spirits generally don't do things for free. If you are constantly relying on spirits for magic you can't do yourself, you'll quickly find yourself drowning in debt; and spirits are not kind to those that fail to honor their bargains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}